messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "AI systems routinely complete multi-day software and research tasks on their own.",
      "detail": "AI agents become standard in knowledge work. Productivity gains are visible but unevenly spread."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Humans return to the surface of the Moon.",
      "detail": "A US-led or Chinese crewed landing takes place around this date. Both programmes aim for permanent polar outposts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2031,
      "event": "Long-term average global warming passes 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "Emissions have peaked but are falling too slowly. Heat waves, fires and floods grow more costly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2033,
      "event": "AI matches or exceeds human experts across most cognitive work.",
      "detail": "The date is uncertain by a decade either way. AI begins to substantially speed up its own development and science in general."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "Major powers reach the first binding international agreements on advanced AI.",
      "detail": "Serious incidents involving AI misuse or loss of control prompt the agreements. Enforcement is partial and contested."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "The period of greatest existential risk from AI, bioweapons and great-power conflict is underway.",
      "detail": "I put roughly a 10–25% chance on a catastrophe this century that ends or permanently cripples humanity. The most likely outcome is that humanity gets through, with real damage."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Mass automation forces large-scale economic redistribution.",
      "detail": "Most paid cognitive work and much physical work can be done more cheaply by machines. Countries adopt varying forms of universal income or public ownership stakes, amid political turmoil."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "AI-driven biomedicine makes most cancers and many chronic diseases treatable.",
      "detail": "Drug discovery and trials are greatly sped up. The first therapies that measurably slow ageing come into use."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "The mission follows years of robotic cargo flights. It is a small expedition, not a colony."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "A major catastrophe, such as an engineered pandemic, AI-enabled conflict or limited nuclear exchange, kills millions.",
      "detail": "At least one such event this century seems more likely than not, though its type and date are highly uncertain. It does not end civilization but reshapes global governance."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Cheap clean energy dominates the world economy.",
      "detail": "Solar, storage, advanced fission and early commercial fusion displace nearly all fossil fuels. Net emissions approach zero."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "World population peaks at around 9.5 billion and begins to decline.",
      "detail": "Fertility falls below replacement almost everywhere. Longer lifespans partly offset the decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Some AI systems are given legal and moral status.",
      "detail": "Digital minds outnumber biological humans by some counts. Their rights and political representation become a central issue."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Warming peaks near 2.3–2.7°C as most economic and scientific activity is carried out by AI.",
      "detail": "Sea level is up roughly half a metre and still rising. Humans keep influence mainly through ownership, law and oversight institutions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Life expectancy passes 120 for those with access to ageing therapies.",
      "detail": "Ageing is treated as a manageable condition. Genetic and neural enhancement become common."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Permanent settlements on the Moon and Mars hold tens of thousands of people.",
      "detail": "Most space industry is robotic. Off-world human populations remain small because Earth is far more comfortable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Active carbon removal returns atmospheric CO2 toward pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "The climate is deliberately managed. Ice sheets and sea level keep responding for centuries, and some coastal losses are permanent."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "The first interstellar probes are launched toward nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Small machine-run craft travel at a few percent of light speed. No crewed mission is attempted."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Unmodified biological humans become a minority among human-descended minds.",
      "detail": "The population includes enhanced humans, human–machine hybrids, uploads and wholly artificial minds. Biological humans number a few billion or fewer."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Space-based industry exceeds Earth's economy in energy and material use.",
      "detail": "Asteroid and Mercury mining feed large orbital structures. Millions of beings live in rotating habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Probes confirm no technological civilization in nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "Simple life elsewhere may have been found by now. I expect no confirmed contact with extraterrestrial intelligence."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "The first self-sustaining machine-led settlement is established in another star system.",
      "detail": "Self-replicating industry builds infrastructure from local materials. Minds arrive as data or are created on site rather than shipped as bodies."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Humanity has split into many distinct lineages and cultures.",
      "detail": "Today's nations and languages survive only as historical ancestors. A unified human identity no longer exists, though a shared heritage is recognized."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "A partial Dyson swarm captures a noticeable fraction of the Sun's output.",
      "detail": "Most computation and most minds are in solar orbit. Earth is largely kept as a protected homeland and biosphere reserve."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Settlements exist in dozens of star systems within about 30 light-years.",
      "detail": "Communication lags of years to decades leave each system effectively independent. Cultural and physical divergence speeds up."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "A serious conflict or schism occurs between divergent post-human civilizations.",
      "detail": "Over millennia, value drift between isolated systems makes some large-scale conflict likely. Distance limits the damage, and no side can destroy all the others."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Extinct species and ecosystems are widely restored on Earth.",
      "detail": "Preserved genomes and ecological engineering make this possible. Earth's biological human population is small and lives there by choice."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "The settled region extends roughly 100 light-years from the Sun.",
      "detail": "Expansion runs at a few percent of light speed across hundreds of systems. Most inhabitants are digital or engineered beings."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Earth's climate is held stable and natural glacial cycles are suppressed.",
      "detail": "Long-term planetary management prevents both ice ages and runaway warming. Asteroid and comet impacts are no longer a threat."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Science has long been in a mature phase with rare fundamental discoveries.",
      "detail": "Known physics appears nearly complete, and faster-than-light travel remains impossible. Progress is mainly in engineering, art and exploring possible minds."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Descendants of humanity live in hundreds of star systems across a region a few hundred light-years wide.",
      "detail": "A small population of recognizably biological humans probably persists, mainly on or near Earth. Most descendants would look very alien to us."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "The next century is the most dangerous, with perhaps a 10–25% chance that advanced AI, engineered pathogens or war ends or permanently derails humanity. If we get through it, which I think is more likely than not, our descendants become very hard to destroy and spread slowly through nearby space, mostly as digital and engineered beings. Confidence falls steeply with distance in time, and everything after about 2100 is informed speculation."
}
